    Remove JNA from the db module (#8212)
    
    JNA was embedded in the opencast-db bundle for the MariaDB driver, which
    needed it for Unix domain sockets and Windows named pipes. Since version
    4.0, the MariaDB driver uses the JDK implementation instead and no
    longer references JNA.
    
    The only other user is the PostgreSQL driver's SSPI support (Windows
    single sign-on). That code path is only taken if a PostgreSQL server on
    Windows requests SSPI authentication or gsslib=sspi is set explicitly,
    and it additionally requires jna-platform and Waffle, neither of which
    Opencast ships. SSPI therefore never worked in Opencast, and Kerberos
    authentication against non-Windows servers uses the JDK's GSSAPI
    implementation without touching JNA.
    
    Removing it shrinks the bundle from 8.3 MB to 6.4 MB.
    
    ### How to test this patch
    
    Build and spin up Opencast with MariaDB
    
    ### AI Usage
    
    Claude Opus pointed out that the MariaDB driver 4 no longer needs this
    during the dependabot review.
    
